        { "do": "Now $f(3)$. Open G-SOLV again: [[SHIFT]] [[F5]].", "keys": ["SHIFT", "F5"],
          "screen": { "type": "graph", "win": [-5, 7, -6, 6], "fns": ["x*x-2*x-4"], "fkeys": ["ROOT", "MAX", "MIN", "Y-ICPT", "ISCT", "▷"] } },
        { "do": "Press [[F6]] (▷) to see more options.", "keys": ["F6"],
          "hint": "The ▷ arrow on F6 means 'more options'.",
          "screen": { "type": "graph", "win": [-5, 7, -6, 6], "fns": ["x*x-2*x-4"], "fkeys": ["Y-CAL", "X-CAL", "∫dx", "", "", "▷"] } },
        { "do": "Press [[F1]] **Y-CAL**.", "keys": ["F1"],
          "screen": { "type": "graph", "win": [-5, 7, -6, 6], "fns": ["x*x-2*x-4"], "label": "Y-CAL", "read": "X:" } },
        { "do": "Type `3` and press [[EXE]].", "keys": ["3", "EXE"], "entry": { "prefix": "X:" },
          "screen": { "type": "graph", "win": [-5, 7, -6, 6], "fns": ["x*x-2*x-4"], "pt": [3, -1], "label": "Y-CAL", "read": "X=3  Y=-1" } },
        { "ask": "What are the $y$-intercept and $f(3)$?",
          "options": ["$y$-intercept $(0,\\ -4)$ and $f(3) = -1$", "$y$-intercept $(-4,\\ 0)$ and $f(3) = -1$", "$y$-intercept $(0,\\ -4)$ and $f(3) = 3$"],
          "answer": 0,
          "why": "The $y$-intercept is where $x = 0$, so it is (0, −4). Y-CAL with X = 3 gives Y = −1." }
      ],
      "result": "$y$-intercept $(0,\\ -4)$ and $f(3) = -1$. Check by hand: $3^2 - 2(3) - 4 = -1$."
    },
    {
